{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"Sunāga","html":"<article id='thag1.85'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Theragāthā 1.85 </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Verses of the Senior Monks 1.85 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Ekakanipāta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Book of the Ones </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Navamavagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Chapter Nine </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Sunāgattheragāthā </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Sunāga </span></h1></header>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Cittanimittassa kovido, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Skilled in the patterns of the mind, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Pavivekarasaṁ vijāniya; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>understanding the nectar of seclusion, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Jhāyaṁ nipako patissato, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>practicing absorption, alert, mindful: </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Adhigaccheyya sukhaṁ nirāmisan”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>such a person would realize pleasure not of the flesh. </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endsutta'><span class='root'>… Sunāgo thero …. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p></article>"}
